<title>USA: Bayer to develop Arris asthma compound.</title>
<headline>Bayer to develop Arris asthma compound.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH SAN FRANCISCO, Calif. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arris Pharmaceutical Corp said Bayer AG plans to develop its tryptase inhibitor known as BAY17-1998, with the goal of entering into clinical trials for the treatment of asthma.</p>
<p>BAY17-1998 is an inhaled therapeutic.</p>
<p>The two are continuing to collaborate on an oral tryptase inhibitor for asthma.</p>
<p>Bayer's decision to develop BAY17-1998 will result in an undisclosed milestone payment to Arris.</p>
<p>&quot;The selection of BAY 17-1998 underscores both companies' belief that the inhibition of the mast cell protease, tryptase, offers a new modality for the treatment of asthma,&quot; John Walker, Arris chief executive said in a statement.</p>
</text>
